      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Longboat men transported goods like indigo and cotton down the Mississippi in the late 18th century, passing through Lake Providence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Providence%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Louisiana State Cotton Museum sits on the lakefront north of town, showcasing the state’s cotton heritage.",
